# RDBMS migration-ledger state. This is NOT build output: unlike the manifest,
# snapshot, and audit trees (which hang off the generated OUTPUT dir, and so land
# in .generated/, outside this repo), `.datrix/rdbms-migrations/` is written back
# into the APPLICATION SOURCE dir and is version-controlled by design. The ledger
# is a deterministic function of the schema so regeneration never churns it,
# revisions are immutable once written, and the documented recovery from a
# wrongly-reset baseline is to restore ledger.json / schema.json / the revision
# file to their COMMITTED bytes. Discarding it would leave a clone unable to
# continue the example's migration chain -- the next run would emit a fresh
# `0001_initial` that a deployed database has already recorded and will never
# apply.
#
# The blanket ignore stays as the stray guard: `commit-and-push` runs
# `git add -A`, so state written by an ad-hoc run against an example that sets
# `migrations { enabled = false }` would otherwise be committed unlooked-at.
# Every example that deliberately sets `enabled = true` is re-negated below.
# Adding another such example means adding a line here -- and this list cannot
# go stale silently, because ignored-source-gate.ps1 fails the commit run until
# it does.
.datrix/
!/examples/03-domains/ecommerce/.datrix/

# Crash / stack dump files
*.stackdump

# Claude Code per-session runtime state. The hook CODE under
# claude-config/.claude/hooks/ is versioned on purpose; the state it writes at
# runtime is not. `.state/mandatory-reads-<session-id>.json` records which gated
# docs one session has read (written by session-context.py at every SessionStart,
# appended by track-mandatory-reads.py, consumed by gate-mandatory-reads.py);
# `scheduled_tasks.lock` holds a live pid + session id. Both are machine- and
# session-local and meaningless in any other clone -- 12 of the former were
# committed by stray `git add .` before this rule existed.
claude-config/.claude/hooks/.state/
claude-config/.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Claude Code's per-machine permission grants. `settings.json` is the shared,
# reviewed project configuration; `settings.local.json` is the file Claude Code
# WRITES BY ITSELF whenever a permission prompt is answered "don't ask again",
# so its contents are whatever commands happened to run on one machine --
# absolute paths outside the workspace, session-scoped temp directories, and
# (this is why it is ignored, not merely untidy) grants naming CUSTOMER cloud
# resources and customer checkout paths, which must never enter a framework
# repo. It was tracked by stray `git add .` and carried exactly that. Nothing in
# it is meaningful in another clone.
claude-config/.claude/settings.local.json

# Temp / scratch / test-output directories must never be created inside a
# package repo at all -- they belong outside the repo tree. This is a backstop
# for the rule, not a licence: a stray `.test-output/` was committed here once.
.test-output/
.test_output/
.tmp/
.temp/
.scratch/
.scripts/
.agent_output/
